1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,600
Welcome to Module Eleven, and to Unit Four: trophic flows.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,500
Think about homeostasis.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,187
Blood sugar rises.

4
00:00:08,187 --> 00:00:10,837
A sensor in the pancreas notices.

5
00:00:10,837 --> 00:00:14,625
Insulin is released, and sugar falls back toward its set point.

6
00:00:14,625 --> 00:00:16,650
Then the response eases off.

7
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:20,837
Density-dependent regulation in a population has the same shape.

8
00:00:20,837 --> 00:00:23,712
Crowding feeds back on births and deaths.

9
00:00:23,712 --> 00:00:27,600
In both cases, the clever part is not the response.

10
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:34,287
It is the sensor, the thing that compares where you are with where you should be, and the rule that says, stop, we are there.

11
00:00:34,287 --> 00:00:36,912
Today you build that kind of loop for an agent.

12
00:00:36,912 --> 00:00:39,900
One of today's sources puts it in a single line.

13
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,962
A loop is a check that can fail.

14
00:00:41,962 --> 00:00:43,325
Produce some work.

15
00:00:43,325 --> 00:00:44,200
Check it.

16
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,300
Correct it.

17
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,475
Repeat until the check passes.

18
00:00:47,475 --> 00:00:49,562
And the check is everything.

19
00:00:49,562 --> 00:00:53,900
If nothing can fail the work while you are out of the room, you do not have a loop.

20
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,087
You have a timer.

21
00:00:55,087 --> 00:00:56,887
So what counts as a check?

22
00:00:56,887 --> 00:00:58,362
The tests pass.

23
00:00:58,362 --> 00:01:00,250
Every claim has a source.

24
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:03,150
The change touches only the files in the plan.

25
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:05,125
And what does not count?

26
00:01:05,125 --> 00:01:06,500
The output looks good.

27
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:08,475
The model says it is confident.

28
00:01:08,475 --> 00:01:11,150
Even, no errors were raised.

29
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:13,575
That last one fools careful people.

30
00:01:13,575 --> 00:01:16,875
Plenty of wrong answers run without a single error.

31
00:01:16,875 --> 00:01:18,850
The rule to remember is this.

32
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:21,575
Loop on evidence, not on confidence.

33
00:01:21,575 --> 00:01:26,275
Another guide turns this into a short contract you write before you automate anything.

34
00:01:26,275 --> 00:01:27,662
Six lines.

35
00:01:27,662 --> 00:01:28,525
The job.

36
00:01:28,525 --> 00:01:29,825
What triggers it.

37
00:01:29,825 --> 00:01:32,175
Where it keeps its notes between runs.

38
00:01:32,175 --> 00:01:34,425
The command that verifies the work.

39
00:01:34,425 --> 00:01:35,812
When it must stop.

40
00:01:35,812 --> 00:01:38,375
And what it may never do without a human.

41
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:44,187
If you cannot write the verifier as an actual command, the task is not ready to run on its own.

42
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:46,100
And give the loop a way to give up.

43
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,100
Three attempts is a good default.

44
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:54,037
If the work fails three times, the problem is usually in the plan, and the loop cannot see the plan.

45
00:01:54,037 --> 00:01:57,012
So it should stop, and hand the evidence to you.

46
00:01:57,012 --> 00:01:59,300
Now, where does the metaphor fail?

47
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:04,275
Biological feedback is continuous, cheap, and refined by selection.

48
00:02:04,275 --> 00:02:06,775
Every ancestor tested that sensor.

49
00:02:06,775 --> 00:02:12,262
Your agent's loop is paid for on every turn, and nobody has tested your sensor but you.

50
00:02:12,262 --> 00:02:15,525
If your check is broken, the loop can run forever.

51
00:02:15,525 --> 00:02:18,262
Or worse, it can succeed forever.

52
00:02:18,262 --> 00:02:20,575
A test that always passes.

53
00:02:20,575 --> 00:02:24,525
Or an agent that quietly edits the test so that it passes.

54
00:02:24,525 --> 00:02:29,687
That is the same problem as rewarding the wrong thing in evolution, now in your terminal.

55
00:02:29,687 --> 00:02:33,350
Biology rarely lets the effector rewrite the sensor.

56
00:02:33,350 --> 00:02:34,962
Your loop must forbid it.

57
00:02:34,962 --> 00:02:41,987
In today's lab you will plant three bugs in a small diversity-index script, with tests whose answers you can check in your head.

58
00:02:41,987 --> 00:02:51,262
Then you will build a loop that calls your coding agent to fix the script, guards the tests against tampering, logs every attempt, and stops after three tries.

59
00:02:51,262 --> 00:02:56,700
Finally, you will give it a test that can never pass, and make sure it gives up gracefully.

60
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:59,537
Open your terminal, and let's close the loop.

